research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:5:The scope here is the geometric and mathematical development of non-Abelian Yang–Mills theory: principal bundles and connection forms; local gauge potentials and curvature; the classical Yang–Mills action; gauge fixing, Faddeev–Popov, BRST and BV; perturbative gauge-preserving renormalization; topological sectors and instantons; lattice observables and confinement; and the four-dimensional existence/mass-gap frontier. General EFT and anomaly-matching interfaces belong to the adjacent scaffold, while supersymmetry transformations, supermultiplets, BPS sectors, localization, and dualities belong to the supersymmetry scaffold. This note proposes a few shared gauge suppliers for those tracks but does not take ownership of their distinct results.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:34:The completed root math run **inverse-problems-knot-theory-all-109-2026-10-19** was checked from the live .autopilot/ status and Git history on 2026-10-23; the run status is COMPLETE. **def-asd-moduli-fredholm-index-and-lattice-setup** and **thm-asd-deformation-complex-index-formula** are root-published but absent from the current physics import snapshot. **thm-charge-one-self-dual-su-two-connections-on-the-round-four-sphere-are-bpst** is a draft and not imported. **lem-euclidean-asd-energy-concentration-is-finite** is an untracked item file, and the weak Coulomb ASD regularity helpers remain drafts outside the physics snapshot. These files are candidate mathematics context only. They do not certify a four-dimensional Yang–Mills quantum theory, a local proof in this physics category, or the completeness of instanton compactness/regularity arguments.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:40:| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory/qft-g02.md**: **post-qft-formal-qed-coefficients**, **post-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-model**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-existence**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-ward**; supporting **def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data** | The finite lattice model is a finite oriented graph with compact \(U(1)\) rotors on links, finite CAR matter, integer electric operators, an explicit Hamiltonian domain and Gauss operators. Its published physical theorems establish a nonzero finite-regulator Gauss sector, unitary dynamics and selected finite-regulator Ward/Gauss identities under their stated assumptions. | This is not non-Abelian \(G\)-valued link data, not an infinite lattice theorem, not a continuum limit, not interacting continuum QED, not a proof of confinement, and not a Yang–Mills existence or mass-gap supplier. The formal QED coefficients are not a convergent series or an all-loop gauge-independence theorem. |
