research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json:2013:      "candidate_contract": "`thm-qftx-n-extended-central-charge-bounds` is a mathematics theorem on a common invariant dense domain in a positive Hilbert-space representation. Use η=(-+++), σ^μ=(I,σ⃗), {Q^I_α, Q̄_{β̇ J}}=−2σ^μ_{αβ̇}P_μδ^I_J, {Q^I_α,Q^J_β}=2ε_{αβ}Z^{IJ}, ε₁₂=1, and the massive one-particle rest-frame fiber P^μ=(M,0,0,0), so P₀=−M. For N=2 with Z¹²=Z, choose φ with e^(−iφ)Z=|Z| and A=Q¹₁−e^(iφ)(Q²₂)†. Prove {A,A†}=4(M−|Z|)I and hence M≥|Z|, with equality forcing the corresponding supercharge combination to annihilate the state. State the dense-domain and adjoint justification; a sharp-momentum eigenstate need not be a normalizable vector in the full Hilbert space. The bound does not prove existence or stability of a state.",
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json:2038:      "proof_supplement": "On the supplied fixed mass/central-charge rest fiber prove positivity of 2[[M I,Z],[Z*,M I]], hence M>=||Z||. For N=2 explicitly expand 4(M-|Z|). Keep the full shortening/multiplicity obligations if claimed; a massless one-particle state is not assigned a rest frame.",
