research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json:5136:      "candidate_contract": "| `exp-aqft-atlas-tau-squark-gluino-search-2025` | ATLAS Collaboration, EPJC 85 (2025) 1437, DOI 10.1140/epjc/s10052-025-14957-6. Search for RPC squark/gluino pair-production simplified models in tau(s)+jets+missing-transverse-momentum: 140 fb⁻¹ at 13 TeV (2015–18) plus 51.8 fb⁻¹ at 13.6 TeV (2022–23); three tau/lepton channels; independently optimized cut-and-count and ML strategies combined in profile-likelihood fits. Paper reports no significant overall deviation, observed 95% CLs exclusions reaching gluino 2.25 TeV / squark 1.7 TeV only in its specific simplified mass parameterizations. | The paper states model-specific spectra, branching fractions, narrow-width approximation, R-parity conservation, detector simulations, trigger selection, tau fake-factor background, jet/tau/lepton calibrations, correlated/uncorrelated nuisances, luminosity uncertainties, and asymptotic profile-likelihood validation. It also reports a locally most-compatible ML benchmark with `p_local=0.00058` (`Z=3.2`) while concluding there is no significant overall deviation; retain this local/background-fit detail and do not turn a local value or contour into a universal SUSY exclusion. Mass limits do not apply to all SUSY models or spectra. |",
