          "source": "lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then $\\Omega_\\omega$ is horizontal and $\\operatorname{Ad}$-equivariant, and $\\Omega_\\omega=\\omega\\circ K_H$ for the imported vertical-valued curvature $K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])$. For any trivializing cover with smooth sections $s_i:U_i\\to P$, set $A_i=s_i^*\\omega$ and $F_i=s_i^*\\Omega_\\omega$. On an overlap, let $g_{ij}:U_i\\cap U_j\\to G$ be the smooth map determined by $s_j=s_i g_{ij}$, and write $\\theta_L(g_{ij})=g_{ij}^*\\theta_L$ for the left Maurer–Cartan form. Then",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "where $(\\rho_*(A_i)\\psi_i)(X)=\\rho_*(A_i(X))\\psi_i$ for $X\\in TU_i$. These expressions patch to a smooth $E$-valued 1-form on $M$, independently of the chosen local sections, and satisfy $\\nabla^\\omega(f\\sigma)=df\\otimes\\sigma+f\\nabla^\\omega\\sigma$ for every smooth scalar function $f$ on $M$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
